# ==========================================
# LINKUP — VERCELIGNORE
# ==========================================
#
# This is NOT a copy of .gitignore, and it does
# a different job.
#
# .gitignore controls what gets COMMITTED.
# This controls what gets SERVED.
#
# They are not interchangeable. Vercel excludes
# .gitignore itself from the deployment output
# but does NOT apply its patterns, so anything
# ignored by git is still published unless it
# is listed here. Only .vercelignore filters
# the static output.
#
# That matters here: supabase-migrations.sql and
# supabase-schema.sql contain the full schema,
# every RLS policy and the body of the
# SECURITY DEFINER functions. ROADMAP.md and
# todos.md are private working notes. None of
# that should be readable at
# https://your-domain/supabase-migrations.sql.
#
# There is no build step and no dependency, so
# there is nothing to compile — the site is
# exactly the HTML, CSS and JS below.


# ------------------------------------------
# Deny everything, then allow only the site.
#
# A denylist is a trap: any dev file added
# later is published by default and nobody
# notices until it is indexed. This fails
# closed instead. If you add a page, add it
# here too.
# ------------------------------------------
/*

!/index.html
!/legal.html
!/favicon.svg

!/app/
!/auth/
!/css/
!/js/
